# loop_eval run-queue lock (#509) — runtime state, never committed
eval/loop_eval/.run.lock

# loop_eval batch outputs (#510/#511) — COMMITTED, deliberately.
# These were ignored as "data, not source" and the b_realm batches were then
# lost: only aggregate stats survived, so the pre-registered residual-failure
# taxonomy (TAXONOMY.md) could never be executed — it labels from transcripts —
# and the headline paired deltas could not be regenerated. A full batch is
# ~4 MB (146 tasks x 4 conditions, transcripts included), which is not a size
# worth trading evidence for. The paper's conclusion also promises the
# per-iteration traces are released.
#   eval/loop_eval/results/
#   eval/loop_eval/manifests/

# loop_eval generated figures (#515) — regenerate via figures.py
eval/loop_eval/figures/
